[enhanced-img]: https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/images#sveltejs-enhanced-img
# Coming from remark and rehype plugins

mdsvex 0.x ran remark and rehype, and took their plugins in `remarkPlugins` and `rehypePlugins`. mdsvex now has its own parser, so those plugins don't run and the two options are gone. Most of what they were used for is built in, an option, or a first-party plugin. Find each plugin you used below, and for one you wrote yourself, see [porting a plugin of your own](#porting-a-plugin-of-your-own).

`migrate_config` from the [migrator](/docs/guides/migrating-from-0x#run-the-migrator) leaves a note for every plugin it finds in your config, with the same answer.

::marks

## Built into the markdown

::::added
:::add[`remark-gfm`, `remark-footnotes`](mark="~~", tone=emph)
built in, apart from one thing: [tables](/docs/learn/markdown#tables), `~~strikethrough~~`, [task lists](/docs/learn/markdown#task-lists) and [footnotes](/docs/reference/footnotes) work as written. A bare url is not linked: the migrator writes each one as `<https://example.com>`, and `references({ linkify: true })` from [`@mdsvex/plugin-references`](/docs/plugins/references) links them all
:::

:::add[`remark-frontmatter`, `remark-parse-yaml`](mark="---", tone=text)
built in: [frontmatter](/docs/guides/frontmatter) is the `metadata` export, and [`frontmatter.parse`](/docs/guides/frontmatter#custom-frontmatter-parsers) takes TOML or full YAML
:::

:::add[`remark-directive`, `remark-admonitions`, `remark-containers`, `remark-custom-blocks`](mark=":::", tone=directive)
built in: [directives](/docs/guides/directives), `:::note` renders your `note` component
:::

:::add[`remark-sub-super`, `remark-supersub`](mark="^", tone=emph)
built in: `H~2~O` and `x^2^`
:::

:::add[`remark-extended-table`, `rehype-merge-cells`](mark="> ^", tone=fence)
built in: a `>` or `^` cell [merges](/docs/learn/markdown#tables), and `||` makes header columns
:::

:::add[`remark-math` with `rehype-katex`, `rehype-katex-svelte` or `rehype-mathjax`](mark="$", tone=code)
built in: a [`math` fence and `` $`x`$ ``](/docs/reference/math), rendered by Temml or, with `math: { renderer: 'katex' }`, KaTeX. For MathJax pass a [function](/docs/reference/math#custom-math-renderers). The migrator rewrites `$x$` when you pass `math: true`
:::

:::add[`remark-code-import`](mark="src=", tone=fence)
built in: [`src=./file.ts#L5-L20`](/docs/reference/highlighting#code-from-a-file) on a fence, the migrator renames `file=`
:::

:::add[`remark-breaks`](mark="\↵", tone=text)
nothing, on purpose: a line end is a space. End a line with a backslash for a break
:::

:::add[`rehype-raw`](mark="<div>", tone=comp)
not needed: HTML in a document is always real markup
:::
::::

## Now an option

::::added
:::add[`remark-smartypants`, and the `smartypants` option](mark="--", tone=text)
an option: [`smart_punctuation: true`](/docs/reference/options#smart_punctuation), off by default
:::

:::add[`rehype-slug`, `remark-slug`](mark="#", tone=heading)
an option: [`heading_ids: true`](/docs/reference/options#heading_ids), which the migrator adds
:::

:::add[`remark-unwrap-images`, `rehype-unwrap-images`](mark="![]", tone=link)
an option: [`unwrap_images: true`](/docs/reference/options#unwrap_images), which the migrator adds
:::

:::add[`mdsvex-relative-images`, `remark-embed-images`](mark="./", tone=link)
on by default: a relative image is [imported](/docs/reference/images), so Vite hashes it
:::

:::add[`remark-link-rewrite`, `rehype-urls`, `remark-prepend-url`, `remark-relative-links`](mark="[]()", tone=link)
an option: [`links`](/docs/reference/links#links) for links between documents and the base path, [`rewrite`](/docs/reference/links#rewrite) for anything else
:::

:::add[`rehype-highlight`, `remark-highlight.js`, `rehype-prism-plus`, `remark-prism`, `@shikijs/rehype`, `rehype-pretty-code`](mark="```", tone=fence)
on by default: [highlighting](/docs/reference/highlighting) needs a theme and no setup. [Fence meta](/docs/reference/highlighting#fence-meta) reads `{1,3-4}`, `/word/` and `showLineNumbers` as they do. For Shiki itself pass a [function](/docs/reference/highlighting#custom-highlighters)
:::

:::add[`rehype-code-titles`, `remark-code-titles`, `remark-flexible-code-titles`](mark="title=", tone=fence)
built in: `title="math.ts"` or `[math.ts]` in the [fence meta](/docs/reference/highlighting#fence-meta)
:::

:::add[`rehype-twoslash`](mark="^?", tone=fence)
an option: [`highlight: { twoslash: true }`](/docs/reference/highlighting#twoslash)
:::
::::

## First-party plugins

::::added
:::add[`rehype-autolink-headings`, `remark-autolink-headings`](mark="#", tone=heading)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-anchors`](/docs/plugins/anchors): `anchors()`, with `heading_ids: true`
:::

:::add[`rehype-external-links`, `remark-external-links`](mark="https:", tone=link)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-external-links`](/docs/plugins/external-links): `external_links({ target: '_blank' })`. 0.x ran this plugin itself, with `rel="nofollow"`, see [what changes](/docs/guides/migrating-from-0x#what-changes)
:::

:::add[`remark-toc`, `rehype-toc`, `@stefanprobst/rehype-extract-toc`, `@vcarl/remark-headings`](mark="::toc", tone=directive)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-toc`](/docs/plugins/toc): `toc()` leaves the headings as data, and `::toc` lists them in the page
:::

:::add[`remark-reading-time`](mark="words", tone=other)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-page-data`](/docs/plugins/page-data): `plugin_data.page.minutes` and `words`
:::

:::add[`rehype-infer-description-meta`, `rehype-infer-title-meta`, `rehype-truncate`](mark="page", tone=other)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-page-data`](/docs/plugins/page-data): `plugin_data.page.excerpt` and `title`, as text
:::

:::add[`rehype-code-group`](mark="tabs", tone=directive)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-tabs`](/docs/plugins/tabs): `:::tabs` around the fences
:::

:::add[`remark-emoji`, `remark-gemoji`](mark=":tada:", tone=text)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-emoji`](/docs/plugins/emoji): `emoji()` turns `:tada:` into the emoji, with GitHub's names
:::

:::add[`remark-github`, `remark-mentions`, `remark-ping`](mark="@user", tone=link)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-references`](/docs/plugins/references): `references({ repo: 'you/site' })` links `@user`, `#123` and commits
:::

:::add[`remark-linkify-regex`, autolink literals](mark="url", tone=link)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-references`](/docs/plugins/references): `references({ linkify: true })` links bare urls
:::

:::add[`rehype-citation`](mark=":cite", tone=directive)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-citations`](/docs/plugins/citations): `:cite[key]` from a CSL JSON file, and `::bibliography`
:::

:::add[`remark-github-blockquote-alert`, `remark-github-alerts`, `rehype-callouts`, `remark-obsidian-callout`, `remark-github-admonitions-to-directives`, `remark-github-beta-blockquote-admonitions`](mark=":::note", tone=directive)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-callouts`](/docs/plugins/callouts): `:::note`, `:::tip`, `:::important`, `:::warning` and `:::caution`. The migrator rewrites `> [!NOTE]` as `:::note`, and leaves a note at Obsidian's other kinds and at a callout that folds
:::

:::add[`remark-validate-links`](mark="404", tone=other)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-link-check`](/docs/plugins/link-check): `link_check()` warns at every link to an id or a document that is not there
:::
::::

## A component or a few lines

::::added
:::add[`rehype-rewrite`, `rehype-wrap`, `rehype-components`](mark="as h2", tone=comp)
a component: [replace the element](/docs/guides/components) with a component of your own
:::

:::add[`rehype-class-names`, `rehype-add-classes`](mark="class", tone=other)
a parse plugin: `{ table: { parse(node) { node.attrs.class = 'table'; } } }` in [`parse_plugins`](/docs/plugins/writing/parse-plugins#parse_plugins)
:::

:::add[`remark-sectionize`, `rehype-section`](mark="##", tone=heading)
a parse plugin: the `sections` plugin under [plugin handlers](/docs/plugins/writing/parse-plugins#plugin-handlers)
:::

:::add[`rehype-figure`, `remark-figure-caption`](mark="figure", tone=directive)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-figures`](/docs/plugins/figures): `:::figure[Caption]` around an image or anything else, with the caption in a `<figcaption>`. A lone image stays an image
:::

:::add[`rehype-img-size`, `rehype-plugin-image-native-lazy-loading`](mark="width", tone=link)
[`@sveltejs/enhanced-img`][enhanced-img] and a component: add `enhancedImages()` to your Vite plugins and every markdown image gets its `width` and `height`, with avif and webp sources, see [optimised images](/docs/reference/images#optimised-images). For `loading="lazy"`, an `img` replacement sets it, and gets the picture as `src`
:::

:::add[`rehype-mermaid`, `remark-mermaidjs`](mark="-->", tone=fence)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-diagram`](/docs/plugins/diagrams): `diagram()` draws each `mermaid` fence, at build time with `pele` installed or in the browser with `mermaid`
:::

:::add[`remark-embedder`, `remark-oembed`, `remark-youtube`](mark="::", tone=directive)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-embeds`](/docs/plugins/embeds): `::youtube[A talk](id=dQw4w9WgXcQ)` and `::vimeo`. Any other site is a leaf directive with a component of your own, see [directives](/docs/guides/directives#the-three-forms)
:::

:::add[`remark-collapse`](mark=":::", tone=directive)
nothing needed: `<details>` and `<summary>` work as typed, with markdown inside, and [`@mdsvex/plugin-elements`](/docs/plugins/elements) adds `:::details[Summary]` and accordions
:::

:::add[`remark-kbd`, `remark-ruby`](mark=":kbd", tone=directive)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-elements`](/docs/plugins/elements): `:kbd[Ctrl]` and `:ruby[漢字](rt=かんじ)`
:::

:::add[`remark-flexible-markers`, `remark-mark-highlight`, `remark-ins`](mark=":mark", tone=directive)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-elements`](/docs/plugins/elements): `:mark[text]` and `:ins[text]`. `==mark==` and `++ins++` are text, a plugin can't add syntax
:::

:::add[`remark-abbr`](mark=":abbr", tone=directive)
[`@mdsvex/plugin-elements`](/docs/plugins/elements): `:abbr[HTML](title="HyperText Markup Language")`
:::

:::add[`rehype-meta`, `rehype-document`](mark="<head>", tone=comp)
a template: a [template](/docs/guides/templates) renders `<svelte:head>` from its props
:::

:::add[`rehype-video`](mark="video", tone=comp)
a component: an `a` or `img` replacement that renders a `<video>` for a video url
:::
::::

## Nothing yet

::::added
:::add[`remark-heading-id`, `remark-attr`, `rehype-attr`](mark="{#id}", tone=expr)
`{#id}` and `{.class}` can't exist, braces belong to Svelte. `heading_ids` makes ids, and a parse plugin can set any attribute
:::

:::add[`remark-definition-list`, `remark-deflist`](mark="<dl>", tone=comp)
type `<dl>`, `<dt>` and `<dd>`
:::

:::add[`remark-wiki-link`](mark="[[ ]]", tone=link)
`[[Page]]` is text
:::

:::add[`remark-lint`](mark="lint", tone=other)
nothing checks style. [`@mdsvex/plugin-link-check`](/docs/plugins/link-check) checks links, and a missing image fails the build when it is [imported](/docs/reference/images)
:::

:::add[`rehype-sanitize`](mark="safe", tone=other)
nothing, and none is planned. A document compiles to a component and runs as code, so don't compile markdown you don't trust
:::

:::add[`rehype-minify`, `rehype-format`](mark="min", tone=other)
not needed, Svelte and Vite own the output
:::
::::

## Porting a plugin of your own

A plugin that is not listed did one of three things. If it changed elements or attributes, a [parse plugin](/docs/plugins/writing/parse-plugins#parse_plugins) can do the same. If it added syntax, a [directive](/docs/guides/directives) is the syntax mdsvex has for that, and plugins can't add more. If it needed to fetch something or read a file while compiling, a plugin does that in [deferred work](/docs/plugins/writing/deferred-work).

Each plate below is a remark pattern, then the same plugin for mdsvex. An mdsvex plugin is an object with a `name` and its handlers under `parse`, passed to `mdsvex({ plugins: [...] })`.

::::plate[`visit` becomes a handler](mark="link", tone=link)
A remark plugin walks the finished tree with `visit`. An mdsvex plugin names the node type instead, and its handler runs for each node of that type while the parser reads the document. A link has its url and its text once it closes, so the handler returns a function that runs then:

```js
// remark
import { visit } from 'unist-util-visit';
import { toString } from 'mdast-util-to-string';

export function vague_links() {
	return (tree, file) => {
		visit(tree, 'link', (node) => {
			if (toString(node).trim().toLowerCase() === 'click here')
				file.message('say where the link goes, not "click here"', node);
		});
	};
}
```

```js
// mdsvex
export function vague_links() {
	return {
		name: 'vague_links',
		parse: {
			link: {
				parse(node, ctx) {
					return () => {
						if (node.text_content.trim().toLowerCase() === 'click here')
							ctx.warn('vague_link', 'say where the link goes, not "click here"', node);
					};
				}
			}
		}
	};
}
```

:::notes
`toString(node)` is `node.text_content`, `node.url` is `node.href`, and `file.message` is `ctx.warn`, which the build prints with the line of the node. A plugin that handles several types has a key for each.
:::

:::edges
- **A handler sees the document up to its node, not past it.** A `visit` that reads ahead becomes a plugin with `sequential: true`, which runs over the finished tree, or a [`document` hook](/docs/plugins/writing/deferred-work).
:::
::::

::::plate[Node types](mark="type", tone=other)
Most mdast types keep their name. These are written differently:

| remark | mdsvex |
| --- | --- |
| `strong` | `strong_emphasis` |
| `delete` | `strikethrough` |
| `inlineCode` | `code_span` |
| `code` | `code_fence` |
| `blockquote` | `block_quote` |
| `listItem` | `list_item` |
| `tableRow`, `tableCell` | `table_row`, `table_cell`, and `table_header` for the header row |
| `thematicBreak` | `thematic_break` |
| `break` | `hard_break` |
| `yaml` | `frontmatter` |
| `textDirective`, `leafDirective`, `containerDirective` | `directive_inline`, `directive_leaf`, `directive_container` |
| `html` | `html` for each element or component, `html_comment` for a comment |

:::notes
A rehype plugin that matched an `element` by its `tagName` keys by what the markdown wrote instead: `a` is `link`, `img` is `image`, and `h1` to `h6` are `heading`, with a `depth`. [Plugin handlers](/docs/plugins/writing/parse-plugins#plugin-handlers) lists every type.
:::

:::edges
- **No handler takes `text`.** A [sequential plugin's `text` function](/docs/plugins/writing/parse-plugins#parse_plugins) rewrites runs of text.
:::
::::

::::plate[Attributes are `attrs`](mark="attrs", tone=comp)
remark sets an attribute through `data.hProperties`, and rehype through `properties`. An mdsvex handler writes it to `node.attrs`:

```js
// remark
import { visit } from 'unist-util-visit';

export function table_class() {
	return (tree) => {
		visit(tree, 'table', (node) => {
			node.data = { ...node.data, hProperties: { className: ['table'] } };
		});
	};
}
```

```js config
// mdsvex
const table_class = {
	name: 'table_class',
	parse: {
		table: {
			parse(node) {
				node.attrs.class = 'table';
			}
		}
	}
};

mdsvex({ plugins: [table_class] });
```

```svx result config
| Plugin | Port |
| --- | --- |
| remark | `attrs` |
```

:::notes
`attrs` takes HTML names, so `class` where rehype has `className`, as one string. On an element that a [replacement](/docs/guides/components) renders, an attribute becomes a prop.
:::

:::edges
- **An element written as HTML keeps what was written on it in `attrs.attributes`.** Set a new object there, in the function the handler returns: `node.attrs.attributes = { ...node.attrs.attributes, class: 'wide' }`.
:::
::::

::::plate[`file.data.fm` becomes `plugin_data`](mark="set", tone=expr, id=file-data-fm)
In mdsvex 0.x a remark plugin added keys to the frontmatter through `file.data.fm`, and the page read them in `metadata`. A plugin now writes with `ctx.set` or `ctx.add`, and the page reads it in `plugin_data`, under the plugin's name:

```js
// remark, for mdsvex 0.x
import { toString } from 'mdast-util-to-string';

export function reading_time() {
	return (tree, file) => {
		const words = toString(tree).split(/\s+/).length;
		file.data.fm.minutes = Math.ceil(words / 200);
	};
}
```

```js config
// mdsvex
const reading_time = {
	name: 'reading_time',
	parse: {
		document(root, ctx) {
			const words = root.text_content.split(/\s+/).length;
			ctx.set('minutes', Math.ceil(words / 200));
		}
	}
};

mdsvex({ plugins: [reading_time] });
```

```svx result config
---
title: A short post
---

It takes {plugin_data.reading_time.minutes} minute to read.
```

:::notes
- **Plugins can't write `metadata`.** It is the frontmatter the author wrote and nothing else, and `ctx.frontmatter` reads it but must not change it. So no plugin can overwrite a key that the author or another plugin wrote, since each plugin writes under its own name. And a page or a [template](/docs/guides/templates#template-props) can tell where a value came from: `metadata.title` was written, `plugin_data.reading_time.minutes` was worked out.
- A template gets both as props, and a [`?data`](/docs/plugins/writing/plugin-data) import gives both to a list of posts.
- A value worked out from the frontmatter or the path alone belongs in `metadata`, through [`frontmatter.parse`](#frontmatter-transforms).
:::
::::

::::plate[Async work goes in `ctx.defer`](mark="defer", tone=expr)
A remark transformer could be async and await anything. An mdsvex handler is synchronous: it starts the work with `ctx.defer(node, task)`, and the task changes the node when it finishes:

```js
// remark
import { visit } from 'unist-util-visit';

export function link_titles() {
	return async (tree) => {
		const links = [];
		visit(tree, 'link', (node) => links.push(node));
		await Promise.all(
			links.map(async (node) => {
				const page = await fetch(node.url).then((r) => r.text());
				node.title = page.match(/<title>(.*?)<\/title>/)?.[1];
			})
		);
	};
}
```

```js
// mdsvex
export function link_titles() {
	return {
		name: 'link_titles',
		parse: {
			link: {
				parse(node, ctx) {
					return () =>
						ctx.defer(node, async (node) => {
							const page = await fetch(node.href).then((r) => r.text());
							node.attrs.title = page.match(/<title>(.*?)<\/title>/)?.[1];
						});
				}
			}
		}
	};
}
```

:::notes
- **No list to collect.** Each link starts its own task, and the Vite plugin waits for all of them before it renders the document. With `compile`, use [`compile_async`](/docs/reference/compile#compile_async).
- **Read files with `ctx.read`, not `fs.readFile`.** It reads through the Vite plugin and makes the file a dependency, so an edit to it compiles the document again. See [loading files](/docs/plugins/writing/deferred-work#loading-files).
:::

:::edges
- **A task changes its own node** and what is inside it. Anything else throws a `TypeError`, where a remark transformer could change the whole tree. Work that needs the whole tree goes in a [`document` hook](/docs/plugins/writing/deferred-work), which may be async.
:::
::::

::::plate[Frontmatter transforms go in `frontmatter.parse`](mark="parse", tone=expr, id=frontmatter-transforms)
A remark plugin that worked a value out of the frontmatter or the path of the file, and wrote it to `file.data.fm`, becomes a `frontmatter.parse`. It gets the text of the frontmatter and `{ filename }`, and what it returns is `metadata`:

```js
// remark, for mdsvex 0.x
export function dated_posts() {
	return (tree, file) => {
		const [, date, slug] = file.filename.match(/(\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})-([^/]+)\.svx$/) ?? [];
		Object.assign(file.data.fm, { date, slug });
	};
}
```

```js config
// mdsvex
import { parse } from 'yaml';

mdsvex({
	frontmatter: {
		parse: (raw, { filename }) => {
			const [, date, slug] = filename?.match(/(\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})-([^/]+)\.svx$/) ?? [];
			return { date, slug, ...parse(raw) };
		}
	}
});
```

```svx result config file="src/posts/2026-11-15-hello-world.svx"
---
title: Hello world
---
```

:::notes
- **It runs wherever the frontmatter is read:** the compiled document, a [`?metadata`](/docs/guides/frontmatter) import and `ctx.frontmatter`. A list of posts sees the same `date` as the page.
- **It replaces the built-in parser,** so it parses the YAML itself, here with `yaml`. See [custom frontmatter parsers](/docs/guides/frontmatter#custom-frontmatter-parsers).
:::

:::edges
- **`filename` is `undefined`** for a document compiled without a path, as `compile()` is without its `filename` option.
- **It sees only the frontmatter.** A value worked out from the body, such as a reading time, is [plugin data](#file-data-fm).
:::
::::
